<p>A DataFrame is a table with labeled rows and columns. The useful skill is not memorizing every pandas method; it is learning a small grammar of operations you can combine.</p>
<section id="learning-goals" class="level2">
<h2 class="anchored" data-anchor-id="learning-goals">Learning goals</h2>
<p>By the end you can:</p>
<ul>
<li>inspect shape, types, and representative rows;</li>
<li>select columns and filter rows without ambiguity;</li>
<li>create derived variables with <code>assign</code>;</li>
<li>summarize groups and reshape results;</li>
<li>join related tables and validate the result.</li>
</ul>
